{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And it was, when the ark set out.</b> He made for it signs before it and after it, to say that this is not its place. And why is it written here? In order to separate between punishment and punishment, etc., as is found in all the Holy Writings (Shabbat 115)." "<b>Arise, YHWH.</b> Because the ark would travel ahead of them a three-day journey, Moses would say: Stand and wait for us, and do not move further away. A consolational teaching in Vayakhel." "<b>And let Your enemies be scattered.</b> Those who are gathered together." "<b>And let those who hate You flee.</b> These are the pursuers." "<b>Those who hate You.</b> These are the haters of Israel, for whoever hates Israel hates Him who spoke and the world came into being, as it is said: ״וּמְשַׂנְאֶיךָ נָשְׂאוּ רֹאשׁ״ (Psalms 83) — and who are they? ״עַל עַמְּךָ יַעֲרִימוּ סוֹד.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:16.647822105Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}